Item #14: photo-task mode + bonus fix to stop_active_timer

Photo task flow:
- load_tasks(subject_id) scans study_materials/<subject>/tasks/task-*.json
  Each task requires task-NN.png to exist and a non-empty accepted[]
  JSON fields: problem (caption text), accepted (list of accepted answers),
  solution_image (filename, defaults to task-NN-solution.png)
- _normalize_task_answer: lowercase + strip punctuation + collapse whitespace
  Match via set-inclusion in normalized space
- Bot sends FSInputFile(task-NN.png) with caption (problem text + prompt)
- User responds with text. Rewards: +3 / +2 / +1 coins by attempt number
- After 3 wrong: send solution image (or text fallback if missing)
- All progress tracked in FSM data (no new DB table)
- Session summary: correct count, total coins, log entry
- Constants exposed: TASK_REWARDS_BY_ATTEMPT, MAX_TASK_ATTEMPTS

Pre-existing bug fix:
- stop_active_timer used to call state.clear() if there was no
  start_time, regardless of state. This wiped MCQ and (now) task
  session state when user typed /stop. Fixed: only touch state if
  current state is TimerStates.active.

Placeholder content for industrial-management:
- task-01.png and task-01-solution.png: 400x250 PNG generated by
  PowerShell + .NET System.Drawing (no Pillow needed). User
  replaces with real images.
- task-01.json: real text problem derived from section-i.txt terms
  ("how do you call the method of continuous time observation").

Stub branch for tasks removed from handle_mode_picked; flashcards
stub remains (waiting for #15).

FSInputFile added to aiogram.types import.

Smoke test: 10 assertion groups covering helpers, FSM state, answer
normalization edge cases, load_tasks behavior, mode discovery
including new "tasks" mode, subjects_with_mode filter, multi-variant
answer matching, backwards compat (15 situational terms + 3 MCQ).

Closes TODO.md #14.
